      "sourceTextSha256": "0f84aeb88630e4020ec26f4a3a857945d5edc2b6b61c82b3c596dc27802b13ce",
      "text": "Day 2 · Corcovado and Christ the Redeemer (4 hours, shared tour). From the station, an eco-friendly train climbs through the jungle to the top of Corcovado, with spectacular views of the Tijuca Forest, home to monkeys and other exotic animals and birds. At 710 metres above sea level stands the symbol of Rio, the 38-metre statue of Christ the Redeemer, built in 1931, with a breathtaking panorama of the city, the Rio–Niterói Bridge, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, Maracanã Stadium and Sugar Loaf.",
